their wards due if any. They must have the record of unpaid students and 
should make them pay the fees on time. 
26. Take necessary steps and motivate the students to get good academic 
laurels. 
27. Tutor is responsible for improving the performance of his / her wards. 
 
28. He / She should play a pro-active role, be friendly and try to achieve 100% 
pass of his / her wards. 
29. If a ward gets low marks / arrears in any subject the tutor should arrange for 
remedial action so that the ward is helped to clear the arrear in the next 
reappearance. 
30. Periodical test marks must be conveyed to the parents. 


